# ON_SHOT — he SHOOTS it and the wish happens the moment he does. A bow, crossbow or trident:
# a beam leaves his eyes along the way he is looking and stops at the first block or creature in its
# way, and the wish happens there — the laser. A wish on HIM happens on him, and the beam is still
# drawn. The weapon shoots its own arrow exactly as it always does; the beam rides the shot.
# WishShapeEvents runs act() as him the tick his arrow leaves the weapon. The beam lines are Java's,
# ShotBeam, filled in where the right-click shapes put their aim.
import common

function give()
${GIVES}
    /tellraw @s {"text":"${GIVE_MESSAGE}","color":"${HEX}"}
end

function act()
    ${AIM}
end

${EFFECT_BLOCK}
